# Draft handoff / source-file transfer (priority backlog)

**Status:** queued 2026-09-29 — Anthony after Steam Cracker ownership discussion. **Do not implement** unless he explicitly restarts this.

Customers (and L&D proponents who hired a contractor) will want the **editable source**, not only a SCORM zip. In NexCourse that source is the **saved draft**, not a Storyline `.story` and not the original PPT.

## What to ship (when restarted)

- **Copy, not co-edit.** Duplicate the draft to another signed-in account so it appears under **their** View drafts. They edit and publish independently. The sender keeps their copy unless they delete it.
- Recipient must already have a NexCourse account (lookup by email).
- Clone `course_drafts` row (new id, their `user_id`) and copy `draft-assets` into their storage prefix.
- Not a review link (play-only, expires). Not Team workspace sharing (same draft, shared). Not “email the zip.”

## Current security (do not weaken)

- Cloud drafts are per-account (`course_drafts.user_id` + private `draft-assets/{userId}/`).
- Other users get 403; RLS is own-row. Review links are temporary player snapshots only.

## Out of scope for this item

- Storing/handing over the original PPT/PDF binary (ingest only; draft JSON + media is the source).
- Vendor lock-in via LMS-redirect SCORM. NexCourse’s point is a real zip **and** an editable draft.
- Live co-authoring on one draft.
